WEBVTT

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.410
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:41.550
The traditional Hakone Academy fun 
ride to send off the third-years

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.660
starts here at this convenience 
store parking lot

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:50.810
<i>RIDE.07  The Last Meet</i>

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.400
once the air's become a little chilly.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:56.760
I never even thought about 
it when we were first-years.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.890
I can't believe we're the 
ones being sent off now.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:06.580
Let's go. It's our last run as part of 
the Hakone Academy bicycle racing club.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.210
Yeah.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.360
Yeah.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.440
It's cold.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.360
I look forward to riding with you today.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.250
Sure.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.210
We're counting on you.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.090
Izumida.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.500
Try not to fall.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.620
Yes, sir.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.040
The third-year send-off 
fun ride will now begin!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.680
Thank you!

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.090
Thank you!

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.530
Make sure you obey all traffic signals.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.450
This 120 kilometer course 
follows the national highway

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.830
and heads south along the coast,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:52.980
turns right at Kawazu, crosses Amagihara 
Pass, and finishes at the city parking lot.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.860
A hundred and twenty kilometers?
Isn't that a little long for a fun ride?

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.520
This is the course we ride every year.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.860
We keep up a brisk pace, 
so try not to fall behind.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.370
What?

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.790
Hakone Academy!

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.370
<b>Toudou
-sama</b>

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.260
Toudou-kun!

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.040
You can do it!

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.830
There are my fangirls.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.940
Thanks for your passionate send-off.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.750
Toudou-sama!

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.080
The last time we'll see his valiant figure!

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.260
You idiot, eyes forward!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.300
<b>Toudou
-sama</b>

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.300
Toudou-kun, point your finger at us!

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.240
The heavens granted me three things.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.150
Not only can I climb, but I'm 
also a skilled conversationalist,

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.480
and then there's my great looks.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.780
Even the forest sleeps through my—

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:39.740
I told you to face forward, you idiot!

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.110
Toudou-san's amazing.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:45.780
Yeah. I don't really get it,
but he's amazing.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.860
No, Toudou actually is amazing.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.160
Fujiwara-senpai!

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.730
Thanks for your three years of service.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.000
Yeah. The next generation of Hakone 
Academy is counting on you.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:00.840
Toudou seems to joke around, 
but when the team needs him,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.060
he always shows up in top condition.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.010
Remember what happened at the Inter-High?

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.330
Yes, sir.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.330
He works hard while we're not watching.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.940
Back-breakingly hard.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.000
Not at all, Fujiwara.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:15.280
What?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.270
It's just the talent heaven has granted me.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.120
I'm what they call a ge—

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.610
Eyes forward!

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.390
What's your problem? That's the best part.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.870
<i>He's kind of annoying.</i>

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.450
Shut up and ride! You're distracting me!

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.460
<i>He really is amazing.</i>

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.790
Thanks, Juichi.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.620
For six years.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.250
Yeah, Shinkai.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:39.190
We've known each other since middle school.
We've been together a long time.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:43.340
It couldn't have been better. 
I'm glad I had you, Juichi.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.680
Thanks to you, I was able to keep riding.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.890
You're the fastest man alive. 
What are you talking about?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:53.080
<i>Amazing. They're recognizing 
each other's abilities.</i>

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.040
<i>And they're strong.</i>

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.060
<i>I want to be like them by 
the time I'm a third-year.</i>

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.940
In order to become strong, you must 
endure the pain and persevere.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.690
I was able to do that for six years because I

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:11.240
had someone as strong as you 
riding beside me, Shinkai.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:12.580
Thank you.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.880
It's embarrassing when you 
put it like that, Juichi.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.300
Want some?

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.660
Don't look at me so expectantly!

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.640
I don't have anything heartfelt to say!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.370
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.870
<i>He doesn't seem the type.</i>

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.140
<i>But how did he know?
Was it his wild instincts?</i>

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:42.730
No, the team came together because of you.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.230
Tou—

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:48.390
Thanks for practicing with us.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.370
Shinkai.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.700
Arakita, no one could've carried us better.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.350
Fuku-chan, you, too?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.170
Shut up! Stop complimenting me!

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:09.300
We're on the seaside highway now.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.010
It's a two-lane road from here on out.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:15.530
Huh? The third-years are moving ahead.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:16.830
It's time.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:17.640
Huh?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.990
This is where it always starts.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.650
But I thought this was a fun ride.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.400
You must be stupid.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.360
Today's course has a finish line,
and we're Hakone Academy.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.360
There's no way it won't turn into a race.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.450
Izumida-san's group is moving ahead, too!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.830
Someone's missing.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.340
It's not a problem. He'll be here soon.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.210
Come, Manami!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.080
Yes, sir.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.390
Even Manami?

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.580
Since I have the opportunity, 
let me be clear.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.990
You are...

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.910
Weak!

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.500
You smeared mud on your 
school's proud history,

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.740
and you failed to win the general 
classification at the Inter-High.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.500
You called yourselves the strongest team,
but placed second!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.500
As far as Hakone Academy is concerned, 
second place is last place!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.480
How are you going to take 
responsibility for that?

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.800
Will you reclaim your honor next year?

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:36.660
You can't. After all, you're third-years.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.810
You're graduating.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:42.160
<i>Izumida...</i>

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:50.290
So we will inherit that 
responsibility and desire!

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.030
Well said.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.290
I used to look up to and chase after you,
but now I will surpass you.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:07.790
Let me show you our strength by 
beating you in your final race!

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.430
Izumida-san zipped up his jersey!

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.670
He's declaring war on the third-years!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.480
Izumida.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.050
Now you've said it.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.810
Kuroda, Ashikiba, and Manami, huh?

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.520
Nice. We should answer their challenge.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.440
Besides...

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:28.730
There it is! It's Shinkai-san's ka-pow pose!

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:32.530
Go, Shinkai!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:35.280
Follow me, Yuki, Ashikiba, Manami!

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.970
Th-They're so fast!

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:41.160
Pedal, first-years!

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.030
If you fall behind now, 
you'll never catch up!

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:45.170
Yes, sir!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.630
Go!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.380
They're so fast.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.030
This isn't good.
They're pulling ahead a little bit.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.260
What should we do, Touichirou?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.040
What? That's not a little.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.270
They're pretty far ahead of us, Yuki-chan.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.490
I wasn't being literal. I meant 
the opposite of what I said.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.100
Learn to read the atmosphere, stupid.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.370
How rude. There's nothing stupid about me.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.710
That's what makes you stupid!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.170
Ninety percent of stupid people
don't realize they're stupid

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.110
and find out from the Ministry of
Internal Affairs and Communications.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.660
Really?

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.790
Of course not! It's a joke!

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:20.710
You should've known!

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.700
D-Do you...

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.500
think I'm one of those people?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.600
I told you, it's not true!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.380
Who would even investigate that?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:33.710
Don't let the name of the Ministry 
make you doubt yourself so much!

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.470
Are you finished with your 
comedy routine, Ashikiba, Yuki?

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.620
For now.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.760
That was a comedy routine?

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.690
What are we going to do?

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:44.970
Follow them, of course.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.020
I'll pull.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.770
I can't lose any more.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:01.370
I can't make the same mistake twice.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.870
I promise I'll win.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.210
I'll pull until my legs fall apart.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.290
I'll catch up to them!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.720
Let me lead us to victory!

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.720
No, it's fine. Head to the back.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.490
Why? I'll pull for us.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:17.450
Fall back.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.550
I know I'm a climber, but—

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.010
What's this?

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:27.230
According to the Ministry's investigation, 
there's another idiot in the group.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.530
He's aloof, smiley, and absent-minded.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:35.330
But he's unbelievably fast on hills.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:39.450
To borrow Arakita-san's words,
he's a wonder boy.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.620
Yuki...

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:50.870
You've been working too hard 
since the Inter-High, Sangaku!

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.670
A first-year shouldn't be shouldering 
that kind of responsibility.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:57.660
Just say there was a pebble in the 
road or make some other excuse.

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:01.180
You pushed past me to attend the Inter-High.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:06.180
You didn't win the group F race 
that day because you had guts.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.850
It was your bottomless focus.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:14.540
But what about now? The burden you're 
carrying is making you unsteady.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:18.500
You're unfocused,
and your pedaling is a mess.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.610
You're a climber, but you 
want to pull on the flats?

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.490
You're supposed to be the guy who says 
he's too tired to pull when he's told to!

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:27.590
<i>Kuroda-san...</i>

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:29.910
Quit putting on airs and working so hard.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.880
Are you trying to look bigger than you are?

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.410
Are you an idol who can't wait to grow up?

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.290
Let the others handle the flats.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.550
These seaside flats will end soon.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.600
There are mountains waiting 
for us after that.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:48.890
That's when we climbers can go wild.

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.830
That's what Touichirou was trying to say.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.460
You finally smiled.

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:04.030
Fall back and rest.
Resting improves your focus.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.570
Right, Manami?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:14.620
Yes, sir.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:18.060
I prepared these for today's race.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:20.020
Is it a map?

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.160
They're number tag stickers.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.210
Wow.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.390
Single digit?

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.680
You're starting to act like 
a captain, Touichirou.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.670
Ace #1, Ashikiba!

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:32.850
You're making me nervous.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:34.680
Number 2, Yuki!

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:37.060
Crap, that's Arakita-san's number.

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.600
Number 3 is for our climber, Manami!

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.070
That's Toudou-san's number.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:46.240
And my number tag is the 
one I've always wanted.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.580
The number of Hakone Academy's
fastest rider, #4!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:52.620
After them!

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.230
Yeah!

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.420
The captain's group is accelerating now!

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:57.890
Follow them!

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:00.420
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:10.630
I thought we had pulled pretty far ahead.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:13.180
That's odd. I guess we hadn't.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.710
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.400
I see them, Touichirou. It's the third-years.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.400
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.410
We'll beat them.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:26.930
Let's go.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:27.910
Yeah!

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.340
Izumida, you know about

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.660
the demon of Hakone that
 appears on straight roads...

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:37.330
Don't you?

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:40.340
Abs! Let's go, Andy!

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.460
Frank!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.170
Come...

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.130
Fabian!

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:53.810
Bring it on, Izumida!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:58.310
<i>My cells are trembling.
My heart won't stop pounding.</i>

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:02.440
<i>I'm about to race against him.</i>

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:06.650
<i>He used to be so far out of reach.
Those days were so long.</i>

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.320
<i>Are you ready?</i>

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:19.290
<i>Show me the best you can do!</i>

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:21.750
<i>Abs, ready...</i>

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.640
<i>Go!</i>

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:30.340
Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.430
It's Hakone Academy's Demon 
of the Straight Road!

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:32.680
Shinkai-san began his counterattack 
after the captain's group caught up!

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:37.230
And Izumida-san reacted instantly 
with his Full-Body Muscle Sprint!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:40.330
Abs! Abs! Abs!

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:39.760
They're both continuing to accelerate!

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:44.540
Such incredible acceleration! 
They're on a different level!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.740
You're a first-year, aren't you?

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.360
Yes, sir. I'm Takadajou.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:55.520
I wanted to experience the third-years' 
last race and how Izumida-senpai rides.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.370
But I can't keep up.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.230
You've got guts.

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.260
Um, what about Shinkai-san and Izumida-san?

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.960
Once we turn right

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:11.340
at the intersection at Kawazu,
the flats of this seaside road will end.

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:15.060
Right under the giant sign in front of it,

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.660
there's a white line that's 
just like a finish line.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:23.590
They'll be riding all-out to that line.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.230
Abs! Abs! Abs!

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.940
Shinkai-san!
 Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:27.940
<i>I will surpass you!</i>

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.610
Izumida!

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.030
Bring it on!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.660
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:15:49.160 --> 00:16:01.520
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:56.180
<i>I'm pulling ahead.
Will you fall behind, Izumida?</i>

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:02.480
<i>My back muscles are the spring.
They're the biggest muscles in the body.</i>

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.370
<i>The back muscles!</i>

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:09.430
<i>They pull the arms through the shoulders 
and turn the legs through the buttocks.</i>

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.970
<i>They're the source of all muscles.</i>

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:17.410
<i>Fierce and grand! The father of all muscles!</i>

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.200
<i>That is Fabian!</i>

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:24.620
Abs! Turn...

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.630
Fabian!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.240
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.630
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:40.700
<i>Izumida, you were a great junior to me.</i>

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:48.570
<i>You were honest, serious, 
and always kept up with me.</i>

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.300
Shinkai-san, may I join you?

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.540
Sure.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:57.250
<i>You were persistent.</i>

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.250
I can't beat him!

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:08.750
Next time, Shinkai-san.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:11.540
Shinkai-san...

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.300
Shinkai-san!

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:21.130
<i>I secretly enjoyed watching you grow.</i>

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:24.100
<i>Shinkai-san!</i>

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:28.570
<i>Five kilometers left.</i>

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.150
<i>We're getting closer.</i>

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:40.950
Abs! Abs! Abs!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.270
<i>Each time my muscles turn the crank...</i>

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.450
<i>Each time my tires kick against the ground...</i>

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.950
<i>I get closer to the end of my time with you.</i>

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.790
<b>Kawazu City</b>

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.790
<i>Two kilometers left.</i>

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:47.040
Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:49.500
<i>One kilometer...</i>

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.500
Abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.860
<i>I will surpass him.</i>

00:17:56.330 --> 00:18:01.300
<i>It's the final stretch. Give me 
your strength, Andy, Frank, Fabian!</i>

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:06.310
<i>Shit, my legs are falling off. But...</i>

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:12.730
Abs! Abs! Abs!

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.190
<i>500 meters left!</i>

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.160
<i>It's the final stretch! Pedal!</i>

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:14.860
<i>That's it!</i>

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:17.170
<i>The finish line!</i>

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:24.990
<i>Why? Why am I crying?</i>

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.220
<i>That's it.</i>

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:40.840
<i>That's it. This is...</i>

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:50.160
<i>...what it means...</i>

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:54.440
<i>...to surpass someone you admire.</i>

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:05.900
<i>You've grown, Touichirou.</i>

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:10.460
I did it! Abs!

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:20.930
Thank you, Shinkai-san.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:29.190
In our final race, I rode 
with your #4 on my chest.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:33.350
Don't steal that. That's my number.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:39.070
But I guess it's time I let you have it.

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.120
Thank you!

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:52.760
I have one last question.

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:57.390
Shinkai-san, why did you smile then?

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:02.050
Yeah, I wonder why.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:08.140
I was just having so much 
fun that I couldn't contain it.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:21.190
The climber and ace stages 
are after this one.

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:22.480
Yes, sir.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.290
Let's have one last race.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.000
Come with me. I'll give 
you a workout, Manami.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:34.670
Yes, sir.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:38.840
It's time.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.030
Huh?

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:43.880
On this course, after the 
right turn at Kawazu...

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:54.140
...waits Amagihara Pass, the tallest 
peak on the Izu Peninsula.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:56.940
Toudou-san and Manami?

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:57.990
That's right.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:21:03.030
You'll never see a race between Hakone 
Academy climbers like this one again.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.990
Not that we'll be able to watch it.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:08.470
Let's ask them how it went later.

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:09.270
Yeah.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:15.450
There's a mountain ahead of us. Let us climb.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:21.920
To the highest point on this road, 
the place closest to the sky.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.430
Let's race to see who gets there first.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:29.730
Don't hold anything back, Manami Sangaku.

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:30.930
Yes, sir.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:33.390
Attack me anytime.

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.890
I'll crush each and every 
one of your attempts.

00:23:13.810 --> 00:23:16.390
Jinpachi, Yasutomo's glaring at you.

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:18.470
I don't mind.

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:21.290
Now, what will you do? 
You're in check, Kuroda.

00:23:22.690 --> 00:23:25.720
Don't let him beat you, Kuroda. Get him.

00:23:26.620 --> 00:23:28.630
The tension is intense.

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:34.450
Usakichi!

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:39.850
<i>NEXT RIDE  Finish Line</i>

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:44.860
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
